      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Request similar to but not the same as\nbeing able to disable physbones:\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-dynamics-reports-and-feedback/p/1181-request-enableactive-property-for-physbones-colliders-and-contacts\nbeing able to grab multiple parts of a bone chain:\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-dynamics-reports-and-feedback/p/can-only-grab-one-part-of-the-same-physbone-hierarchy-at-a-time\n(as these likely require similar features. eg: being able to freeze a physbone and/or have multiple calculation points)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-24T20:52:08.687Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "My suggestion is to allow physbones to have some sort of anchor, either at multiple points through the bone chain or at least at the end of a bone chain.\nThis would allow for simulating pocket chains, a secured wire/cord, straps, a necklace, etc. Essentially to create a \"loop\".\nI have been trying for quite a while now to create any sort of anchor or constraint that functions for any of these but have been unable to. Unity constraints dont work (parent, position, etc). Creating an inside boundary collider to contain the last bone in a chain doesnt work. Ignoring transforms on the last bone, making that a physbone and setting it to be completely immoble doesnt work. Making only half of a loop physbones and then using rotation constraints to simulate the second half of the loop *almost* works (if you create the armature very very carefully and hinge constraints you can poorly simulate a loop but it needs very specific conditions). The closest you can get is a cloth object currently but that has a litany of disadvantages and struggles to simulate anything stiff.\nThe physbones as added to VRC work fantastically, but this is definitely my primary complaint with them at the moment, it is impossible to create any sort of loop as far as I can tell.",
